# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Environment Variables Example (.env.example)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# 1. LOCAL USE:
#    - Copy this file and rename it to `.env`:
#        cp .env.example .env
#    - Paste your Personal Access Token below.
#    - Benefits: Avoids GitHub API unauthenticated rate limits (5,000 req/hr
#      instead of 60 req/hr) and fetches your private repository stats.
#
# 2. GITHUB ACTIONS CLOUD CI/CD:
#    - To let the GitHub Actions automated workflow fetch private repo stats
#      and higher rate limits in the cloud, add this token as a GitHub Secret:
#        1. Go to your repo: https://github.com/<username>/<username>
#        2. Click 'Settings' -> 'Secrets and variables' -> 'Actions'
#        3. Click 'New repository secret'
#        4. Name: GH_TOKEN
#        5. Value: <your-personal-access-token>
#        6. Click 'Add secret'
#
# 3. HOW TO GENERATE A GITHUB TOKEN:
#    - Go to GitHub -> Settings -> Developer Settings -> Personal access tokens -> Tokens (classic)
#    - Click 'Generate new token (classic)'
#    - Scopes to select:
#        - `repo` (Full control of private repositories - required for private stats)
#        - `read:user` (Read user profile data)
#
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Your GitHub Personal Access Token (PAT)
GH_TOKEN=ghp_your_personal_access_token_here

# Alternatively, you can use GITHUB_TOKEN
# GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_your_personal_access_token_here
